From openbsd-alpha  Fri Jul 19 00:30:47 2002
From: Marc Matteo <marcm () lectroid ! net>
Date: Fri, 19 Jul 2002 00:30:47 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: port can't find its own library
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=102703874803955

Hi all,

I've been trying to compile a recently posted (to ports@) port of Pango
(part of GTK+2) on an Alpha but it fails when /usr/bin/ld complains it
can't find a shared library that it just finished compiling.

It exists, I checked, and the -L options should cover it... but ld can't
seem to find it.

Short of me screaming at the screen "It's right there, stupid!" I'm at a
loss.

Strange as it is, if I change the library's name from
"libpango-1.0.so.0.3" to "libpango.so.0.3" and call it with "-lpango"
instead of "-lpango-1.0" it works.

Can anyone point me in the right direction on this?

Thanks,
Marc

P.S.: I'm attaching a portslogger output for those that might find it
useful.
