 > On Thu, Jul 11, 2002 at 12:27:34PM +0200, Matthieu Herrb wrote:
 > | The support for VGA cards on OpenBSD/alpha has just been added a
 > | couple of days ago. You should wait for the next snaphot including X
 > | and try it. 
 > 
 > Could you give an indication where I can find more info on this
 > subject ? Snooping around XF4 sources in cvsweb is quite a challenge
 > with XF4 sources totalling over 50 MB

Look at XF4/distrib/notes/README.alpha were I added information about
the cards I could test. Other reports are welcome. 

The actually enabled drivers are defined in
XF4/xc/config/cf/xfree86.cf. 

And the alpha specific code is mostly in those 2 files:
XF4/xc/programs/Xserver/hw/xfree86/common/compiler.h
XF4/xc/programs/Xserver/hw/xfree86/os-support/bsd/alpha_video.c

It also uses code from the newly added libalpha in
src/lib/libarch/alpha. 

 > I'm particularly interested in which VGA cards will work with these
 > changes (3dFX Voodoo Banshee perhaps ?).

I think the tdfx driver has been tested on Linux/alpha. So it should
work on OpenBSD too (provided you have a BWX capable machine for
now). 

					Matthieu

